brian a las vegas man is left to plan  not only one funeral but three he spoke  to victoria saha and how in just a blink  of an eye covid took his family away  32 year old jason rose has dealt with  more loss in the last week than most  people do in a lifetime he is struggling  to find ways to come to terms with the  loss of his grandfather grandmother and  mother he says it's just a reminder of  how quickly this virus can take away  lives rose's grandparents and mother  went into the hospital together last  week by friday they had all died his  mother was a high risk dialysis patient  and was going through dialysis every day  at home she worried the side effects of  the vaccine would do more harm than good  his grandparents were hoping faith would  get them through this pandemic it's  unclear how they contracted the virus  but now rose is left to pick up the  pieces  my grandpa passed on tuesday  this past tuesday  and then you know my grandma passed away  thursday and then my mom passed away  friday morning to be honest i'd rather  have been me you know like that's how  much i love my family rose also dealt  with covid earlier this summer and was  unvaccinated he says he is more inclined  to get the vaccine now  rose is planning funeral services and is  trying to save the home his mother  bought 22 years ago her dying wish was  to hold on to that house he has set up a  gofundme in hopes to get help it's on  our website at 8newsnow.com victoria  saha 8 news now
 

